			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Implement NativeHostService and platform detection across Mountain, Wind, and Sky\n\nCoordinate three Land submodules to add VS Code compatibility layer with native OS integration:\n\n- **Mountain**: Add ProcessPolyfill commands (getExecPath, getPlatform, getArch, getPid, getShellEnv, getMemoryInfo) and NativeHostService interface with file system operations (URI normalization, userdata path resolution ~/.land/User/...), native dialogs (pickFolderAndOpen, showOpenDialog), OS properties via sysinfo crate (dark mode detection across macOS/Windows/Linux, PTY profile detection), clipboard, window state, power management, and storage service. Add SharedProcessProxy health checks.\n\n- **Wind**: Add DetectPlatform() for browser-side OS/arch/hostname/release detection. Update CreateProcess and ResolveConfiguration with platform-specific values for PATH, execPath, homeDir, tmpDir, userDataDir. Rename Tauri commands from colon format (`process:get_exec_path`) to underscore format (`process_get_exec_path`) to match Mountain's Tauri 2.x command names. Add proper error propagation for file system errors.\n\n- **Sky**: Bump astro 6.1.4 → 6.1.5; remove auto-generated .astro/build artifacts.\n\nThese changes enable the VS Code workbench to access native OS features and communicate correctly with Mountain via Tauri IPC.",
			"SHA": "4d133ba74c13b8412efde6fbb57e50190a949a75"
		}
